<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.10.4: Rewriting Expressions in Vertex Form</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02503</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.10.4: Rewriting Expressions in Vertex Form</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d256145f-a67b-40ca-97c5-71d91548fb23</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>Here is one way to rewrite <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00001">vertex form (of a quadratic expression)</term>.</item>
      </list>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00001">Study the steps and write a brief explanation of what is happening at each step.</para>
          <para id="para-00002">Original expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00003"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00004"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00005"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00006"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00007"><emphasis>Step 5</emphasis> - <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00008">Write down your answers, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00009">Compare your answers:</para>
          <para id="para-00010">Original expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00011"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Rewrite the expression with 3 as a factor. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00012"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Add 4 to complete the square. Subtract 4 to keep the value of the expression the same. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00013"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Combine like terms so we can see the perfect square, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00014"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Rewrite <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> as a squared expression. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00015"><emphasis>Step 5</emphasis> - Apply the distributive property to put the expression in vertex form. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_94449039-e496-4222-9357-adb316d75f6e" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00016">Enter the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex.</para>
          <para id="para-00017">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00002">vertex (of a graph)</term> that represents this expression?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00018">Correct! The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex is -2.</para>
          <para id="para-00019">Nice try! The correct answer is -2. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex is -2.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="f18e0bfe-9bca-49e0-9491-9ba2737676f3" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00020">Enter the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex.</para>
          <para id="para-00021">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph that represents this expression?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00022">Correct! The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex is -3.</para>
          <para id="para-00023">Nice try! The correct answer is -3. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex is -3.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00024">Does the graph open upward or downward? Explain how you know.</para>
          <para id="para-00025">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00026">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00027">The graph opens upward. For example, in an earlier unit, we saw that when the coefficient of the squared term <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is positive, the graph opens upward.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00028">Rewrite <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in vertex form.</para>
          <para id="para-00029">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00030">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00032">Rewrite <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>24</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in vertex form.</para>
          <para id="para-00033">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00034">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00036">Rewrite <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in vertex form.</para>
          <para id="para-00037">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00038">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Are you ready for more?</title>
      <section id="sect-00003">
        <title>Extending Your Thinking</title>
        <exercise id="ab222ab2-5d97-49df-8acc-336fae8e8aa4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            <para id="para-00040">Fill in the missing parts of the function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> in vertex form <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:munder><m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi mathvariant="bold">a</m:mi><m:mo mathvariant="bold">.</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/></m:mrow><m:mo accent="true">―</m:mo></m:munder><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:munder><m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi mathvariant="bold">b</m:mi><m:mo mathvariant="bold">.</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/></m:mrow><m:mo accent="true">―</m:mo></m:munder><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:munder><m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi mathvariant="bold">c</m:mi><m:mo mathvariant="bold">.</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/></m:mrow><m:mo accent="true">―</m:mo></m:munder><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:munder><m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi mathvariant="bold">d</m:mi><m:mo mathvariant="bold">.</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/></m:mrow><m:mo accent="true">―</m:mo></m:munder><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:munder><m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi mathvariant="bold">e</m:mi><m:mo mathvariant="bold">.</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/></m:mrow><m:mo accent="true">―</m:mo></m:munder></m:mrow></m:math> without completing the square. (Hint: Think about finding the zeros of the function.)</para>
            <para id="para-00041">Enter the value of a.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00042">Correct! 2</para>
            <para id="para-00043">Nice try! The correct answer is 2.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_277518af-2d92-470c-ac83-5496e448abd3" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00009">
            <para id="para-00044">Enter the sign of b.</para>
            <para id="para-00045">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00046">Subtraction(-)</para>
            <para id="para-00047">Addition(+)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00048">Correct! Minus (-)</para>
            <para id="para-00049">Nice try! The correct answer is minus (-)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_8cd977bb-ada8-403c-8e9c-4081c87392f6" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00010">
            <para id="para-00050">Enter the value of c.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00010">
            <para id="para-00051">Correct! 6</para>
            <para id="para-00052">Nice try! The correct answer is 6.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_910680bf-69a5-4f48-96ca-d0497eb75ee5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00011">
            <para id="para-00053">Enter the sign of d.</para>
            <para id="para-00054">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00055">Subtraction(-)</para>
            <para id="para-00056">Addition(+)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00011">
            <para id="para-00057">Correct! Minus (-)</para>
            <para id="para-00058">Nice try! The correct answer is minus (-)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="fef2672c-3097-4539-a128-fbe4c56b1a3a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00012">
            <para id="para-00059">Enter the value of e.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00012">
            <para id="para-00060">Correct! 18</para>
            <para id="para-00061">Nice try! The correct answer is 18.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise class="RFM1" id="exer-00006">
          <problem id="prob-00013">
            <para id="para-00062">Be prepared to show your reasoning for your answers.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00013">
            <para id="para-00063">Enter your explanation.</para>
            <para id="para-00064">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00065">The zeros of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are 3 and 9. Because the graph of a quadratic function has a vertical line of symmetry across the vertex, the vertex of the graph must have <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate 6. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex is -18 because <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>18</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. This means <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> can be expressed as <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>18</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. If we expand <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, we can see that the coefficient of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is 2. This means that <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in the vertex form has to be 2 as well.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <!--End interaction-->
        <exercise id="_02de0598-1fa0-4520-ba6e-37d0ac19e22d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00014">
            <para id="para-00066">Fill in the missing parts of the function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>21</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in vertex form <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:munder><m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi mathvariant="bold">a</m:mi><m:mo mathvariant="bold">.</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/></m:mrow><m:mo accent="true">―</m:mo></m:munder><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:munder><m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi mathvariant="bold">b</m:mi><m:mo mathvariant="bold">.</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/></m:mrow><m:mo accent="true">―</m:mo></m:munder><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:munder><m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi mathvariant="bold">c</m:mi><m:mo mathvariant="bold">.</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/></m:mrow><m:mo accent="true">―</m:mo></m:munder><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:munder><m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi mathvariant="bold">d</m:mi><m:mo mathvariant="bold">.</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/></m:mrow><m:mo accent="true">―</m:mo></m:munder><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:munder><m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mi mathvariant="bold">e</m:mi><m:mo mathvariant="bold">.</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/></m:mrow><m:mo accent="true">―</m:mo></m:munder></m:mrow></m:math> without completing the square.</para>
            <para id="para-00067">Enter the value of a.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00014">
            <para id="para-00068">Correct! 2</para>
            <para id="para-00069">Nice try! The correct answer is 2.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="fba80e14-fdbf-4f0d-8703-583700f83fd9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00015">
            <para id="para-00070">Enter the sign of b.</para>
            <para id="para-00071">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00072">Subtraction(-)</para>
            <para id="para-00073">Addition(+)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00015">
            <para id="para-00074">Correct! Minus (-)</para>
            <para id="para-00075">Nice try! The correct answer is minus (-)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d3a81070-2192-4244-b09c-b289636dca8c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00016">
            <para id="para-00076">Enter the value of c.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00016">
            <para id="para-00077">Correct! 6</para>
            <para id="para-00078">Nice try! The correct answer is 6.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_01da4daa-5e72-4557-9a2e-2df9526aa50b" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00017">
            <para id="para-00079">Enter the sign of d.</para>
            <para id="para-00080">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00081">Subtraction(-)</para>
            <para id="para-00082">Addition(+)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00017">
            <para id="para-00083">Correct! Plus (+)</para>
            <para id="para-00084">Nice try! The correct answer is plus (+)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="e362abd6-cf29-48ab-b377-849f9629b625" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00018">
            <para id="para-00085">Enter the value of e.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00018">
            <para id="para-00086">Correct! 3</para>
            <para id="para-00087">Nice try! The correct answer is 3.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise class="RFM1" id="exer-00007">
          <problem id="prob-00019">
            <para id="para-00088">Be prepared to show your reasoning for your answers.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00019">
            <para id="para-00089">Enter your explanation.</para>
            <para id="para-00090">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00091">Although 3 and 9 are not zeros of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 3 and when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 9, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is 21, or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>21</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. Because the graphs of quadratic functions are symmetric, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex is still 6. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex is 3 because <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. The value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 2 for the same reason as in function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
    <!--End interaction-->
    <section id="sect-00004">
      <title>Video: Rewriting Expressions in Vertex Form</title>
      <para id="para-00092">Watch the following video to learn more about rewriting expressions in vertex form.</para>
      <media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text">
        <iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f4900a114d3f80ff7308afc6c3831e2d1db15424"/>
      </media>
    </section>
    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
      <para id="para-00093">Write <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in vertex form.</para>
    </note>
    <section id="sect-00005">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>
      <section id="sect-00006">
        <title>Vertex Form with a Leading Coefficient Besides 1</title>
        <para id="para-00094">Write <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00003">vertex form (of a quadratic expression)</term>.</para>
        <para id="para-00095">Original expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00096"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Rewrite the expression with 2 as a factor. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00097"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Add 4 to complete the square. Subtract 4 to keep the value of the expression the same. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00098"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Combine like terms so we can see the perfect square, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00099"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Rewrite <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> as a squared expression. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00100"><emphasis>Step 5</emphasis> - Apply the distributive property to put the expression in vertex form. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <note class="try" id="note-00002">
          <title>Try It: Vertex Form with a Leading Coefficient Besides 1</title>
      <exercise id="exer-00008">
            <problem id="prob-00020">
              <para id="para-00101">Write <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>24</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in vertex form.</para>
              <para id="para-00102">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00020">
              <para id="para-00103">Here is how to write the quadratic expression in vertex form:</para>
              <para id="para-00104">Original expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>24</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00105"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Rewrite the expression with 4 as a factor. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00106"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Add 9 to complete the square. Subtract 9 to keep the value of the expression the same. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00107"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Combine like terms so we can see the perfect square, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00108"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Rewrite <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> as a squared expression. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00109"><emphasis>Step 5</emphasis> - Apply the distributive property to put the expression in vertex form. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>24</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            </solution>
          </exercise>
        </note>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>